BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventartatnoon3afelixgonzaleztorresatglenstone22249-20261120@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261119T185738Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Art at Noon: Felix Gonzalez-Torres at Glenstone
DESCRIPTION:Associate Curator Yuri Stone will present on four recent installations of work by Felix Gonzalez-Torres at Glenstone Museum. One of the most significant artists to emerge out of New York City in the late 1980s and early 1990s\, Gonzalez-Torres is best known for using everyday materials to evocatively express both the personal and the political. The Cuban-born American artist transformed lightbulbs\, clocks\, and candies into refined\, at times participatory\, sculptures that reflect themes of partnership\, love\, loss\, and intimacy. Friday\, November 20 • 12–1 pm FREE
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/art-at-noon%3a-felix-gonzalez-torres-at-glenstone/22249/
END:VEVENT
